  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Current satellite imagery as of 130 AM \nPDT this morning depicts ample low stratus clouds across the \nforecast area. Expecting patchy freezing fog to develop this \nmorning as well, primarily within valleys where cloud cover \nbreaks and mostly clear skies become present before sunrise. \nOtherwise weather will be fair today under high pressure. Daytime \nhigh temperatures will be slightly warmer than yesterday, residing\nin the upper 40s to upper 50s. For tonight, anticipating mostly \nclear skies and light to calm winds which will help promote the \nformation of freezing fog within most of the valleys across the \nforecast area given the recent rainfall event. Overnight low \ntemperatures will be in the 20s, with mid to upper teens in the \ntypical colder valleys. Fair weather and gradual warming trend \ncontinues thru Sunday. \n\nBy Sunday night, numerical model guidance remains consistent in a\nmodest low pressure system moving into the PacNW. The cold front\nassociated with this system looks to move into northern Nevada\nfrom the west-northwest on Monday. Light valley rain and mountain\nsnow showers are forecast beginning Monday afternoon and thru\nMonday night with valley rain likely transitioning to a rain/snow\nmix overnight. Not anticipating any significant precipitaton\naccumulation with this event and totals will likely remain around\na tenth of an inch or less. Southwesterly breezes will also be \npresent on Monday in conjunction with the passing cold front. \n\nFair weather returns Tuesday and persists thru mid week with\nseasonal temperatures. Potential for precipitaton returns to the \nforecast in the Thursday night to Friday time frame as another \nPacific trof is indicated to move into the western U.S.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence \nregarding a gradual warming trend into Monday. Moderate forecast \nconfidence in the possibility of valley rain and mountain snow in \nNorthern Nevada Monday afternoon thru Monday night. \n\nVarious model blends and WPC guidance utilized for PoP and \nweather fields.",
